From 33b2c4ab6ad2aae272fa97f839abbcb47c577435 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Claude <noreply@anthropic.com>
Date: Mon, 28 Sep 2026 20:19:09 +0000
Subject: [PATCH] Nibe drift: real-time operating-data page (prio, compressor
 power/frequency/current, pump speeds, degree minutes, temps)
MIME-Version: 1.0
Content-Type: text/plain; charset=UTF-8
Content-Transfer-Encoding: 8bit

Håkan asked for "driftdata, vad som sker för sekunden" — the existing
Dashboard NibeStatusCard (30s-cached last-decision summary) and
NibeHistoryCharts (hourly trends) don't show what the compressor is
doing right now. New GET /api/nibe/live reads the F750's real-time
entities straight from HA (prio, compressor power/mean-power/current/
frequency/state, charge- and supply-pump speed, electric addition,
degree minutes) alongside the existing settings/last-decision status,
read-only — same "zero I/O except history+live" convention as
core/nibe/history.py. New /nibe page combines the live card with the
existing history charts; both stay on the Dashboard too, unchanged.

Along the way: NibeStatusCard/useNibeStatus had their own stale local
copies of the heating/DHW status label maps, missing 5 status values
Fas 4c/4d/4e added (engaged_price_spike_ahead, reduced_expensive_price,
blocked_low_degree_minutes, suppressed_anti_flap,
forced_normal_legionella_guard) — pulled into a shared
lib/nibeStatusLabels.ts both now use, fixing the staleness bug.

Also fixes the frontend's hand-written lucide-react ambient module
declaration (src/types/lucide-react.d.ts), which was missing
Thermometer/Droplet/Gauge and silently masked the real package's
types for every icon.

Co-Authored-By: Claude Sonnet 5 <noreply@anthropic.com>
Claude-Session: https://claude.ai/code/session_01D9yfcLt9RHbqoZD18y9PT7
